<article class="env-lemma" id="05V7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05V7">Lemma <span data-tag="05V7">18.37.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $p$ be a point of $\mathcal{C}$ or of its associated topos. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The functor $p_* : \textit{Ab} \to \textit{Ab}(\mathcal{C})$, $A \mapsto p_*A$ is exact. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
There is a functorial direct sum decomposition 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  p^{-1}p_*A = A \oplus I(A)  \]
</div>
<p>
 for $A \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\textit{Ab})$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/05UX" data-tag="05UX">7.32.9</a> there are functorial maps $A \to p^{-1}p_*A \to A$ whose composition equals $\text{id}_ A$. Hence a functorial direct sum decomposition as in (2) with $I(A)$ the kernel of the adjunction map $p^{-1}p_*A \to A$. The functor $p_*$ is left exact by Lemma <a href="/tag/03DC" data-tag="03DC">18.14.3</a>. The functor $p_*$ transforms surjections into surjections by Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/05UY" data-tag="05UY">7.32.10</a>. Hence (1) holds. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>